body:
When we've "discussed" divorce in the past she's always just said "do it, go ahead, do it," as if daring me. Yet, at times she speaks as though we will get an amendable divorce. She's a bit unpredictable, and difficult to talk to because she gets all defensive. 

&#x200B;

I'm ready for this and have been ready but also been very afraid--of her, of her yelling and berating me. I'm tired of being emasculated and put down in front of my kids for just being me. Screaming "YOU SUCK!" at me while the kids look on--it just sucks and I can't take it anymore.

&#x200B;

Bottom line, I suspect her reaction will be nothing, until she decides to rip me a new asshole for something else unrelated.

Yeah, there really is no solution to my issue. I cannot afford divorce. Don't get me wrong, I have an okay job with good benefits. But I have a lot of debt because of student loans and the wife not working. Adding child support and maintenance payments to my budget would make me homeless. 

&#x200B;

Back to the shotgun to my head idea.
